# mutter -- the GNOME compositor, and the first package in this tree that is a
# desktop rather than a library.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. BLFS
# 12.4 is the book this desktop tier follows and it carries 48.4, which is the
# GNOME 48 series this whole chain targets.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/mutter/48/mutter-48.4.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=1189cf7e63cc87cfdd1f3a86e8f14d97c33d6a9da254f23e81655549b6c50d93
SRC_DIR=mutter-48.4

# EVERY EXPENSIVE OPTION IN THIS PACKAGE DEFAULTS TRUE, so most of what follows
# is turning things OFF or confirming that ON is affordable. meson.options:
# sound_player, profiler, libgnome_desktop, libwacom, startup_notification,
# opengl, x11, wayland, xwayland, remote_desktop and introspection are all true
# by default; only egl_device and docs are false and tests is auto.
#
# -Dprofiler=false. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE and it is A HARD FAILURE WEARING AN
# ESCAPE HATCH. meson.build 452-469 takes sysprof-capture-4 with
# `required: true` AND a `fallback: ['sysprof', ...]`. The fallback reads like
# an escape, and _scripts/build-meson.sh passes --wrap-mode=nodownload, which
# turns every fallback into decoration -- so with sysprof unpackaged this is a
# configure failure, not a soft skip. It is a developer profiling hook and not a
# desktop feature; nothing is lost.
#
# -Dx11=false, -Dxwayland=true. This tree runs NO X SERVER -- the README says so
# and there is no Xorg in the package set. -Dx11 gates mutter running as the
# compositor of a NATIVE X11 session, which could never start here. Xwayland is
# an X server rooted under the Wayland session and is packaged.
#
# THE TWO ARE NOT INDEPENDENT, and the line that decides it is meson.build:138:
#
#     have_x11_client = have_x11 or have_xwayland
#
# so X CLIENT support stays on via xwayland even with x11 false. That is why
# startup-notification is packaged and why libX11 and friends are still needed:
# X applications running under Xwayland are real, only a native X session is not.
#
# XWAYLAND IS A HARD BUILD REQUIREMENT DESPITE APPEARING OPTIONAL. meson.build
# 611-621 takes dependency('xwayland', required: false) -- soft -- and then
# falls back to find_program('Xwayland').full_path(), which has NO
# required:false and is fatal when absent. So -Dxwayland=true needs xwayland
# packaged, which it now is. NOT setting -Dxwayland_path: it would satisfy
# configure with a path to a binary that need not exist, producing a mutter that
# builds green and cannot start Xwayland at runtime.
#
# -Dsound_player=true, its default, and the four packages behind it are why the
# sound wave exists: libcanberra (meson.build:193) plus libvorbis, libogg and
# the freedesktop sound theme. The theme is a separate package that nothing
# joins to the player at build time -- with the player and no theme every
# desktop event is silent and no check anywhere says so.
#
# -Dlibgnome_desktop=true, its default. meson.build:187 resolves
# dependency('gnome-desktop-4') -- the GTK 4 library, which is what
# gnome-desktop's -Dbuild_gtk4 produces and the reason that package precedes
# this one.
#
# -Dlibwacom=true, its default. Graphics-tablet support; libwacom is packaged
# and gnome-control-center requires it unconditionally anyway, so it must exist
# regardless of what this flag says.
#
# -Dstartup_notification=true, its default, live via have_x11_client above.
#
# -Dremote_desktop=true, its default: it needs pipewire and libei, both
# packaged. This is also what mutter's screencast path uses, which is the half
# that breaks first if it is missing.
#
# -Dtests=disabled. The option is a FEATURE defaulting to `auto`, so it would
# switch itself on wherever it found what it needs -- finding 4's shape. The
# suite wants a running compositor and reference output; it is not what CI is
# for here.
#
# -Dopengl=false, AND THIS IS A CORRECTION. An earlier version of this recipe
# left it alone with the note "-Dopengl and -Dwayland are true and must stay
# so". CI disagreed on both architectures:
#
#     Run-time dependency gl found: NO (tried pkgconfig and system)
#     mutter-48.4/meson.build:198:11: ERROR: Dependency "gl" not found
#
# meson.build 195-198 takes dependency('gl') unconditionally under -Dopengl, and
# `gl` means DESKTOP OpenGL via gl.pc, whose entry point is libGL -- which is
# the GLX library. THIS TREE HAS NO libGL AT ALL: pkgs/mesa/pkg.env says so in
# as many words, "mesa is built with -Dglx=disabled because nothing here runs an
# X server, and libGL is the GLX entry point -- desktop OpenGL is reachable only
# through EGL", and that comment names mutter as the reason it is correct.
#
# So the answer was already written down in this tree and I asserted the
# opposite without reading it. The flaw is the same one that cost libcanberra a
# cycle one package earlier: I examined the option and asked whether it was
# WANTED rather than whether it was SATISFIABLE HERE. "Must stay so" was a
# statement about GNOME in general, not about this target.
#
# -Dgles2 and -Degl stay at their defaults of true, which is the combination
# mesa's comment describes: mutter renders through EGL and GLES and scans out
# through GBM, none of which needs GLX.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately: -Ddocs and -Degl_device are already false upstream, and
# -Dwayland is true and must stay so. Recorded rather than passed so a future
# default flip reads as a change rather than as a silent new dependency.
#
# FLOORS WITH ZERO HEADROOM, checked against the tree and recorded because a
# configure failure around any of them is a FLOOR question and not a recipe bug:
#     wayland-protocols >= 1.41   tree 1.41.0   EXACT
#     libgudev          >= 238    tree 238.0.0  EXACT
#     libdisplay-info   >= 0.2    tree 0.2.0    EXACT
#     wayland-server    >= 1.23   tree 1.23.1   one patch level
# Everything else has room. And one floor that LOOKS broken and is not: mutter
# wants udev >= 228 while this tree ships eudev 3.2.14 -- eudev's configure.ac
# sets AC_SUBST(UDEV_VERSION, 251) deliberately, so its udev.pc advertises 251
# and the floor is met.
MESON_ARGS="-Dprofiler=false -Dx11=false -Dxwayland=true \
-Dsound_player=true -Dlibgnome_desktop=true -Dlibwacom=true \
-Dstartup_notification=true -Dremote_desktop=true \
-Dintrospection=true -Dtests=disabled \
-Dopengl=false -Dgles2=true -Degl=true"
